Package: granola-for-linux
Version: 0.1.0
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: camarigor <igor@marques-it.tech>
Depends: p7zip-full, libnss3, libatk1.0-0, libatk-bridge2.0-0, libcups2, libdrm2, libxkbcommon0, libxcomposite1, libxdamage1, libxfixes3, libxrandr2, libgbm1, libasound2, libpango-1.0-0, libcairo2, libgtk-3-0, libgl1, libglx-mesa0, libegl1
Homepage: https://forgejo.tinfoilhat.work/camarigor/granola-for-linux
Description: Run the Granola client (macOS/Electron) on Linux
 Ships the Electron runtime plus the stubs for the macOS native modules needed
 to load the Granola client on Linux.
 .
 This package does NOT distribute Granola. On first run it extracts the app from
 the official .dmg that the user downloaded from granola.ai.
 .
 Status: Phase 1 (the interface loads). Audio capture depends on a native module
 that has not been ported yet - see docs/findings.md in the repository.
